<h1>gamepad_remove_mapping</h1>
<p>This function can be used to remove the current device mapping from the given gamepad slot index. Once called, the slot index will need to be remapped using the <a href="gamepad_test_mapping.htm"><span class="inline">gamepad_test_mapping()</span></a> function if you want to be able to be able to use the gamepad constants to detect input correctly (direct input can always be retrieved using the <span class="inline"><a href="gamepad_axis_count.htm">gamepad_axis</a>/<a href="gamepad_button_count.htm">button</a>/<a href="gamepad_hat_count.htm">hat_count()</a></span> and <span class="inline"><a href="gamepad_axis_value.htm">gamepad_axis</a>/<a href="gamepad_button_value.htm">button</a>/<a href="gamepad_hat_value.htm">hat_value()</a></span> functions together).</p>
<p> </p>
<h4>Syntax:</h4>
<p class="code">gamepad_remove_mapping(index);</p>
<table>
<tbody>
<tr>
<th>Argument</th>
<th>Type</th>
<th>Description</th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>index</td>
<td><span data-keyref="Type_Real"><a target="_blank" href="../../../GML_Overview/Data_Types.htm">Real</a></span></td>
<td>Which gamepad index &quot;slot&quot; to remove the mapping from.</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p> </p>
<h4>Returns:</h4>
<p class="code"><span data-keyref="Type_Void">N/A</span></p>
<p> </p>
<h4>Example:</h4>
<p class="code">if (remap == true)<br/>
{<br/>
    gamepad_remove_mapping(global.PadIndex);<br/>
}</p>
<p>The above code will remove the mapping from the given gamepad index slot based on the value of a variable.</p>
<p> </p>
<p> </p>
